# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in what you need. A variable set in the shell wins over this
# file. Every entry is optional.

# Voices. A script names only its provider (voice: kokoro | openai | elevenlabs); how each provider
# sounds is set here, once, for every video. A speed is a number from 0.8 to 1.2; absent means 1.

# Kokoro runs locally and needs no key. af_ = American female, am_ = male, bf_ / bm_ = British.
# KOKORO_VOICE=af_heart
# KOKORO_SPEED=

# OpenAI needs a key; the voice is one of alloy, ash, coral, sage, verse, … Instructions set the tone.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_VOICE=alloy
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# OPENAI_INSTRUCTIONS=calm, confident developer demo
# OPENAI_SPEED=

# ElevenLabs needs a key and a Voice ID (from the voice's page; not a secret, but the account's own).
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE=
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_multilingual_v2
# ELEVENLABS_SPEED=
# A pronunciation dictionary, as <dictionary id>/<version id>, applied to every line (how
# Kubermeister is said, for one); the ids come back when the dictionary is created.
# ELEVENLABS_DICTIONARY=

# The app checkout to film, as an absolute path. Default: ../kubermeister next to this repository.
# KUBERMEISTER_APP=/Users/you/Projects/Kubermeister/kubermeister

# The chrome-headless-shell Remotion renders with. Default: the newest one Playwright installed.
# KM_SCREENCASTS_BROWSER=

# 1 removes the kept demo cluster and seeds a new one on the next run.
# KM_SCREENCASTS_FRESH=1

# 1 prints the stack trace with a failure.
# KM_SCREENCASTS_DEBUG=1
